#ROOMS

#49500
"Tangled Swamp"
"Dark, twisted roots break through the muddy banks to the north and south,
jutting into the swamp like the crooked fingers of ancient men.  A fetid
stench rises in gray vapor from the surface of the stagnant water; the
very air smells of decay.  The sickly marsh plants bend under their own
weight--a heavy canopy of twisted branches hangs overhead, the leaves
sparse and frail.  The swamp heads east and west.
"
""
