S

#49501
"Tangled Swamp"
"The swamp seems to have undercut the banks to the north and south, which
have collapsed, forming a north-south trail that leads onto land.  The
stagnant waterway is choked with low, tangled plants that are
unidentifiable in their gray sickness.  To the east and west the swamp
continues.
"
""
