#49502
"Tangled Swamp"
"Ancient, dead trees rise in all directions, their hollow, ashen trunks
eaten by age and weather and parasites.  The frail, soggy wood looks like
ancient paper, and seems about as sturdy.  To the south, a slope of
fallen earth leads into the stagnant waters of a dark, tangled swamp, and
to the east, the trees are too thick to be passed through.  To the north
and west the dead, muddy forest continues.
"
""
