#49505
"Bend in the Tangled Swamp"
"Although this swamp might have been a river at one time, the flow of
water has stopped entirely, leaving a calm, stagnant swamp filled with
dying plants.  This is a bend in the ancient riverbed, where the water
turned east and south through the high, muddy banks.  To the west stands
a huge tree, its roots stretching out like claws.
"
""
